# netsurf: window is a Window -- [object Window], Window.prototype first,
# WindowProperties, the TEMPORARY / PERSISTENT constants (patch 273)
# Generated 2026-10-13
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 272)
#
# Object.prototype.toString(window) gave "[object global]": QuickJS-ng puts
# an own @@toStringTag "global" on its global object (Node's word; no browser
# has one), and window's first prototype was the bridge's WANT census object
# (macsurf_qjs.c qjs_install_want_probe), not Window.prototype. In browsers
# window -> Window.prototype (@@toStringTag "Window", TEMPORARY 0 /
# PERSISTENT 1, also on Window) -> WindowProperties (the named-properties
# object, @@toStringTag "WindowProperties") -> EventTarget.prototype.
#
#  - vita_polyfill.js, last section: the global's own tag is deleted; the
#    census object moves up into the named-properties object's place (it
#    still sees every name a page looks for and does not find -- its
#    has / get continue on its own prototype), so the chain is Chromium's;
#    idempotent (the polyfill can run twice in a realm).
#
# Found by hsw-compare.py (docs/wasm-hcaptcha-measurement.md, "Record,
# replay"); Chromium given [object global] still passes hCaptcha, so this
# is a standards fix, not the refusal.
#
# Gate: testpages/pages/JS-window-proto.html (WINPROTO 6/6, Chromium 6/6;
# the build before fails 1-5).
diff --git a/content/handlers/javascript/quickjs/vita_polyfill.inc b/content/handlers/javascript/quickjs/vita_polyfill.inc
index 2780097b5..f122fed70 100644
